faf_version: "3.0"
project:
  name: mcp-trinity
  goal: A reference MCP server for the three things servers keep reinventing — project context, persistent memory, and agent identity — through the two exposure surfaces already in the ecosystem (Server Card _meta, ai-catalog sibling entries).
  main_language: TypeScript
  type: mcp
stack:
  runtime: Node.js
  build: TypeScript (tsc)
  backend: Node.js (stdio MCP server)
  api_type: MCP (JSON-RPC 2.0 over stdio)
  frontend: slotignored  # no UI layer — stdio reference implementation
  css_framework: slotignored  # no UI
  ui_library: slotignored  # no UI
  state_management: slotignored  # stateless server, memory lives in project.fafm
  database: slotignored  # no database — memory is a file, not a DB
  connection: slotignored  # no database
  hosting: Docker / any Node host — stdio for local, stateless Streamable HTTP for remote
  cicd: GitHub Actions (typecheck + test)
tech_stack: [TypeScript, "@modelcontextprotocol/sdk", yaml, hono]
human_context:
  who: MCP host and server implementers who want project context, memory, and agent identity without inventing their own ad-hoc shape for each.
  what: A minimal reference MCP server exposing project context (.faf), persistent memory (.fafm), and agent identity (.fafa) through the two exposure surfaces already in the ecosystem — the Server Card _meta block and a self-published ai-catalog.json. Dual transport (stdio + stateless Streamable HTTP). The three IANA-registered formats are the worked example.
  why: MCP servers have no standard answer to "who am I, what do I remember, what's my project", so every server that wants it invents one. This pattern already runs in production at faf.one and context.faf.one, but that's a full app — not something you can read in one sitting and fork. This is the minimal, legible, published version.
  where: github.com/Wolfe-Jam/mcp-trinity
  when: "2026-08-12"
  how: TypeScript on the MCP SDK. remember/recall are real file-backed reads/writes proven across a process boundary. See PLANET-FAF/DEV-NOTES/PLAN-mcp-trinity-aaif-40.md for the build plan.
key_files: [package.json, README.md, src/server.ts, src/faf/parse-fafm.ts, demo.ts]
